<p>Before proceeding with the delivery handover, a thorough <strong>Pre-Delivery Inspection (PDI)</strong> is conducted to ensure that the vehicle meets the agreed upon standards and is in a suitable condition for the next owner.</p>

<div style="display: grid; grid-template-columns: repeat(auto-fit, minmax(280px, 1fr)); gap: 20px; margin-top: 24px;">
  <div style="background: rgba(15, 23, 42, 0.75); border: 1.5px solid rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.08); border-radius: 14px; padding: 24px 20px; box-shadow: 0 10px 25px rgba(0,0,0,0.35); transition: transform 0.2s ease, border-color 0.2s ease;">
    <div style="display: inline-flex; align-items: center; justify-content: center; width: 42px; height: 42px; border-radius: 10px; background: #f59e0b22; color: #f59e0b; font-weight: 800; font-size: 1.05rem; margin-bottom: 14px;">01</div>
    <h3 style="color: #ffffff; font-size: 1.1rem; font-weight: 700; margin-bottom: 10px; line-height: 1.4;">Daylight Condition Re-inspection:</h3>
    <p style="color: #94a3b8; font-size: 0.88rem; line-height: 1.65; margin: 0;">This inspection is carried out while the vehicle is in daylight to provide a clearer visual assessment of the condition and any potential issues.</p>
  </div>
  <div style="background: rgba(15, 23, 42, 0.75); border: 1.5px solid rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.08); border-radius: 14px; padding: 24px 20px; box-shadow: 0 10px 25px rgba(0,0,0,0.35); transition: transform 0.2s ease, border-color 0.2s ease;">
    <div style="display: inline-flex; align-items: center; justify-content: center; width: 42px; height: 42px; border-radius: 10px; background: #10b98122; color: #10b981; font-weight: 800; font-size: 1.05rem; margin-bottom: 14px;">02</div>
    <h3 style="color: #ffffff; font-size: 1.1rem; font-weight: 700; margin-bottom: 10px; line-height: 1.4;">Against Pickup Photos:</h3>
    <p style="color: #94a3b8; font-size: 0.88rem; line-height: 1.65; margin: 0;">The inspector compares the current vehicle condition with the photos taken at the pickup location to ensure there have been no significant changes or damages since the vehicle was initially inspected.</p>
  </div>
  <div style="background: rgba(15, 23, 42, 0.75); border: 1.5px solid rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.08); border-radius: 14px; padding: 24px 20px; box-shadow: 0 10px 25px rgba(0,0,0,0.35); transition: transform 0.2s ease, border-color 0.2s ease;">
    <div style="display: inline-flex; align-items: center; justify-content: center; width: 42px; height: 42px; border-radius: 10px; background: #3b82f622; color: #3b82f6; font-weight: 800; font-size: 1.05rem; margin-bottom: 14px;">03</div>
    <h3 style="color: #ffffff; font-size: 1.1rem; font-weight: 700; margin-bottom: 10px; line-height: 1.4;">Odometer Verification:</h3>
    <p style="color: #94a3b8; font-size: 0.88rem; line-height: 1.65; margin: 0;">The inspector verifies the vehicle's odometer reading against the details provided in the LR bilty (Loading Run Bill of Lading) to ensure accuracy and prevent any mismatch.</p>
  </div>
</div>

<p>Once the pre-delivery inspection is complete, the process of handing over the vehicle to the recipient involves several steps:</p>

<ul style="list-style: none; padding-left: 0; margin: 18px 0;">
<li style="margin-bottom: 10px; display: flex; align-items: flex-start; gap: 10px;"><i class="fas fa-check-circle" style="color: #10b981; margin-top: 5px; flex-shrink: 0; font-size: 0.95rem;"></i><span><strong>Destination Inspection:</strong> The recipient is responsible for conducting a checklist-based inspection of the vehicle under daylight conditions.</span></li>
<li style="margin-bottom: 10px; display: flex; align-items: flex-start; gap: 10px;"><i class="fas fa-check-circle" style="color: #10b981; margin-top: 5px; flex-shrink: 0; font-size: 0.95rem;"></i><span><strong>Signature on LR Bilty:</strong> The recipient signs the LR bilty, confirming that they have inspected the vehicle and are satisfied with its condition.</span></li>
<li style="margin-bottom: 10px; display: flex; align-items: flex-start; gap: 10px;"><i class="fas fa-check-circle" style="color: #10b981; margin-top: 5px; flex-shrink: 0; font-size: 0.95rem;"></i><span><strong>Odometer Verification:</strong> The recipient provides the odometer reading for verification purposes, ensuring it matches the value recorded during the pickup.</span></li>
<li style="margin-bottom: 10px; display: flex; align-items: flex-start; gap: 10px;"><i class="fas fa-check-circle" style="color: #10b981; margin-top: 5px; flex-shrink: 0; font-size: 0.95rem;"></i><span><strong>Signed Condition Sign-off:</strong> Both the recipient and the handler sign the condition sign-off sheet, acknowledging that the vehicle meets the agreed-upon standards and is in the condition documented during pickup.</span></li>
</ul>

<p>The signed condition sign-off serves as a protocol ensuring transparency and accountability throughout the entire transportation process.</p>

<p>If any discrepancies or damages are discovered during the destination inspection, the recipient should promptly document them on the condition sign-off sheet and communicate these issues to the handler. The handler will then investigate the matter and resolve any concerns before finalizing the process.</p>

<p>Upon resolving the issues and obtaining the necessary approvals, a new condition sign-off will be prepared, reflecting the resolved conditions and signed by both parties.</p>

<p>The destination inspection and sign-off process ensures that any potential problems or damages are addressed and resolved before the vehicle is handed over to the recipient, preventing any confusion or disputes later on.</p>

<p>By following these steps, the destination inspection and sign-off process guarantees that the vehicle is delivered in the condition documented during pickup, ensuring customer satisfaction and maintaining the integrity of the transportation process.</p>

<p>Furthermore, it helps maintain transparency between the transportation company, the handler, and the recipient, fostering trust and cooperation among all parties involved.</p></div>
    </div>
  </div>
</section>



